      "content": "Yes, that's a valid concern, but it's not a hard and fast rule that all proxies will be highly correlated with race. And even if they are, it's not like you're intentionally trying to redline people. It's just that, in many urban areas, there's a strong correlation between socioeconomic factors and racial demographics. So, if you're using proxies like median household income or education levels, you might be capturing some of that underlying racial bias. But, you can mitigate this by using techniques like data preprocessing, feature engineering, and model selection to minimize the impact of these correlations.",
